  "row_count": 20,
  "notes": {
    "raw": "\\*Data except enthalpy of formation at 298 K estimated. \nPhase changes: 544.59 K, melting point of Bi; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 2.700$ kcal/mol. \n1837 K, boiling point of Bi to equilibrium mixture of Bi(g) and Bi₂(g). \nHeat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations: \n298.15-3000 K: $Cp^{\\circ} = 19.683 + 0.092 \\times 10^{-3} T - 1.789 \\times 10^{5} T^{-2}$ \n$H^{0}-H_{298}^{0}=19.683\\times10^{-3}T+0.046\\times10^{-6}T^{2}+1.789\\times10^{2}T^{-1}-6.473$ \nReaction equations (kcal/mol): \n298.15-544.59 K: $\\Delta \\mathrm{Hr}^{\\circ} = 9.496 + 4.694 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} - 6.678 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 264.800 \\mathrm{T}^{-1}$ \n$\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = 9.496 - 4.694 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} \\ln \\mathrm{T} + 6.678 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 132.400 \\mathrm{T}^{-1} + 25.587 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T}$ \n544.59-1837 K: $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = 3.943 - 0.366 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} - 0.592 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 866.000 \\mathrm{T}^{-1}$ \n$\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = 3.943 + 0.366 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} \\ln \\mathrm{T} + 0.592 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 433.000 \\mathrm{T}^{-1} + 6.207 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T}$ \nSource: Data based on Prusaczyk (101) who estimated molecular constants. ",
    "lines_raw": [
      "\\*Data except enthalpy of formation at 298 K estimated.",
      "Phase changes: 544.59 K, melting point of Bi; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 2.700$ kcal/mol.",
      "1837 K, boiling point of Bi to equilibrium mixture of Bi(g) and Bi₂(g).",
      "Heat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations:",
      "298.15-3000 K: $Cp^{\\circ} = 19.683 + 0.092 \\times 10^{-3} T - 1.789 \\times 10^{5} T^{-2}$",
      "$H^{0}-H_{298}^{0}=19.683\\times10^{-3}T+0.046\\times10^{-6}T^{2}+1.789\\times10^{2}T^{-1}-6.473$",
      "Reaction equations (kcal/mol):",
      "298.15-544.59 K: $\\Delta \\mathrm{Hr}^{\\circ} = 9.496 + 4.694 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} - 6.678 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 264.800 \\mathrm{T}^{-1}$",
      "$\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = 9.496 - 4.694 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} \\ln \\mathrm{T} + 6.678 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 132.400 \\mathrm{T}^{-1} + 25.587 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T}$",
      "544.59-1837 K: $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = 3.943 - 0.366 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} - 0.592 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 866.000 \\mathrm{T}^{-1}$",
      "$\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = 3.943 + 0.366 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} \\ln \\mathrm{T} + 0.592 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 433.000 \\mathrm{T}^{-1} + 6.207 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T}$",
      "Source: Data based on Prusaczyk (101) who estimated molecular constants."
